  { q: 'How do I convert an oven temperature from Fahrenheit to Celsius?', a: 'Use C equals F minus 32, times five, divided by nine. So 350 Fahrenheit is 176.7 Celsius, commonly rounded to 180 on oven dials, and 400 Fahrenheit is about 205 Celsius. The Best Answer Hub Cooking Converter shows the exact value and the usual dial rounding together.' },
